WEBVTT

00:00:20.979 --> 00:00:23.815
And finally, I'm sure you've all noticed

00:00:23.899 --> 00:00:26.193
the fabulous chandelier
you'll be delivering.

00:00:26.276 --> 00:00:27.819
What? Where?

00:00:27.903 --> 00:00:29.029
Up there.

00:00:30.239 --> 00:00:31.240
Nice.

00:00:31.323 --> 00:00:32.950
It's extremely delicate,

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:35.244
so if one of you breaks it,
you're paying for it!

00:00:35.327 --> 00:00:36.620
- Fry did it!
- Did what?

00:00:36.703 --> 00:00:38.664
Just practicing for later.

00:00:41.708 --> 00:00:43.669
Ah, perfect timing.

00:00:43.752 --> 00:00:46.964
I just turbocharged
the ship's matter compressor.

00:00:47.047 --> 00:00:48.465
What's the matter compressor?

00:00:48.549 --> 00:00:50.217
Nothing's the matter, Fry,

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:53.053
now that I've turbocharged
the matter compressor.

00:00:53.136 --> 00:00:55.389
Instead of making
the ship faster,

00:00:55.472 --> 00:00:57.558
how about installing some seat belts?

00:00:57.641 --> 00:00:59.268
Seat belts are dead weight.

00:00:59.351 --> 00:01:01.979
I feel the need for speed!

00:01:02.062 --> 00:01:05.232
Yes, but I feel the nafety for safety.

00:01:05.315 --> 00:01:07.901
Oh, fuff!
I don't get all up in your business

00:01:07.985 --> 00:01:09.820
when you upgrade your bazooms!

00:01:09.903 --> 00:01:13.574
That's because my bazooms
don't put anyone's life in danger!

00:01:15.701 --> 00:01:17.494
Done broke my spine.

00:01:17.578 --> 00:01:18.704
Nice rack, though.

00:01:18.787 --> 00:01:20.205
Thank you, Scruffy.

00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:32.901
Oh!

00:01:32.985 --> 00:01:35.612
You wrecked my dear ship Bessie!

00:01:35.696 --> 00:01:37.739
I just finished naming her.

00:01:37.823 --> 00:01:39.074
Never mind the ship.

00:01:39.157 --> 00:01:40.284
What about us?

00:01:43.787 --> 00:01:44.788
Fry did it!

00:01:46.081 --> 00:01:48.250
We've had it
with this flying slaughterhouse.

00:01:48.333 --> 00:01:50.085
We're having it towed away for scrap,

00:01:50.168 --> 00:01:52.504
and we're getting a new, safer ship.

00:01:56.008 --> 00:01:58.760
Here I comes to save the days.

00:02:04.975 --> 00:02:07.227
This is how you treat me?

00:02:07.311 --> 00:02:10.731
After all the good news I've given you
over the years?

00:02:10.814 --> 00:02:14.276
Well, if you don't want Bessie,
you don't want me.

00:02:14.359 --> 00:02:15.444
Good-bye!

00:02:25.245 --> 00:02:26.788
Don't worry, shippums,

00:02:26.872 --> 00:02:29.958
with a whole junkyard
of spare parts to work with,

00:02:30.042 --> 00:02:32.586
I'll turn you into a tepid rod.

00:02:33.629 --> 00:02:36.048
Oh, what the heck, a hot rod!

00:02:38.342 --> 00:02:39.801
Ooh! Ooh!

00:02:44.014 --> 00:02:47.559
Ah, time for the mornings meltsdowns.

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:54.983
I'll pay you back, I swear.

00:02:55.067 --> 00:02:57.444
Yeah, yeah, I heards its befores.

00:03:02.282 --> 00:03:05.285
Next up, the Planet Expresses ship.

00:03:07.871 --> 00:03:11.667
Whoa, whoa, whoa! Whats the...

00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:13.627
In your face, sucker!

00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:17.631
Also, I'll send you a check
for the parts I stole!

00:03:17.714 --> 00:03:20.050
Okays, ya honest young punk!

00:03:20.759 --> 00:03:22.719
Now ons to the next junker.

00:03:34.648 --> 00:03:36.650
Ah, the open road!

00:03:36.733 --> 00:03:38.860
Not a ship ahead of me.

00:03:43.907 --> 00:03:45.742
Yo, Methuselah, speed it up!

00:03:45.826 --> 00:03:49.830
You're making the roads unsafe
for us maniac street racers!

00:03:49.913 --> 00:03:51.957
Step off, you greasers!

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:55.585
I was street-racing back when
ships still ran on moon water!

00:03:55.669 --> 00:03:58.588
Damn, yo, get a load of speed geezer!

00:03:59.756 --> 00:04:01.049
Hey!

00:04:01.133 --> 00:04:02.843
That's it, you hoodlums!

00:04:02.926 --> 00:04:05.721
Your mouth just wrote
a PayPal transfer request

00:04:05.804 --> 00:04:08.515
that your butt has
insufficient funds to honor!

00:04:08.598 --> 00:04:10.309
Yo, it is on!

00:04:10.392 --> 00:04:11.685
Before that, it was off.

00:04:11.768 --> 00:04:13.353
Twice around Central Park.

00:04:13.437 --> 00:04:17.190
Loser has to make the winner's
Medicare copayments for a year!

00:04:17.274 --> 00:04:18.317
A'ight.

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:19.901
On three. One...

00:04:22.321 --> 00:04:24.281
Aw, it just got real.

00:04:24.364 --> 00:04:26.658
So real I don't believe it.

00:04:26.742 --> 00:04:27.743
...two...

00:04:31.455 --> 00:04:34.916
Aw, man, I can't afford
no Medicare copayments!

00:04:35.584 --> 00:04:37.919
...three!

00:04:51.058 --> 00:04:52.225
Whoa!

00:04:54.227 --> 00:04:56.480
Wrinkles got some mad moves, yo.

00:04:56.980 --> 00:04:59.358
Yo, Wrinkles, you got big glasses.

00:04:59.441 --> 00:05:00.776
I'm gonna call you the Professor.

00:05:00.859 --> 00:05:03.362
What? No one calls me that!

00:05:06.490 --> 00:05:09.952
Hey, Minx, we survive this,
can I finally get that date?

00:05:10.035 --> 00:05:11.995
Nah. You know I'm with Benny.

00:05:12.079 --> 00:05:13.538
Girl, he don't own you!

00:05:13.622 --> 00:05:16.750
Yeah, but he saved me
from my abusive father.

00:05:16.833 --> 00:05:18.961
Not physically abusive, verbally.

00:05:19.044 --> 00:05:22.089
It's a long story I can't get into
while we're spinning out.

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:50.325
Ow! Paper cut!

00:05:51.743 --> 00:05:52.744
Whoa!

00:05:53.954 --> 00:05:57.833
Hey, Earl, it's that street-racing gang
we've been trying to bust for years.

00:05:57.916 --> 00:05:59.501
Unsuccessfully, I might add.

00:05:59.584 --> 00:06:02.462
Guess this is your lucky day, Pimparoo.

00:06:03.005 --> 00:06:06.425
Those punks have endangered our citizens
for the last time.

00:06:10.095 --> 00:06:11.722
Ironic!

00:06:15.142 --> 00:06:16.810
Whoa, it's the police!

00:06:16.893 --> 00:06:18.312
Let's turn and burn!

00:06:23.025 --> 00:06:24.610
Running off, eh?

00:06:24.693 --> 00:06:25.736
You're pathetic!

00:06:25.819 --> 00:06:29.531
You wouldn't be scared of the po-po
if you had a ship like mine.

00:06:29.615 --> 00:06:33.827
Yo, Professor, if your ship's so dope,
why are those cops on your tail

00:06:33.910 --> 00:06:36.913
like my dad's verbal abuse on my psyche.

00:06:36.997 --> 00:06:39.916
'Cause you haven't seen
what old Bessie can do yet.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:42.669
Sayonara, Tokyo driftwood!

00:06:51.261 --> 00:06:53.347
- What the what?
- Whoa, snap!

00:06:53.430 --> 00:06:55.265
Dude pulled a dimensional drift!

00:06:57.935 --> 00:06:59.853
I can't believe we lost them again.

00:06:59.937 --> 00:07:00.938
I need a drink.

00:07:01.021 --> 00:07:03.148
Nah. We're on the job.

00:07:03.231 --> 00:07:05.734
Let's just go pepper-spray
some homeless families.

00:07:14.284 --> 00:07:16.078
That was a sick move, yo!

00:07:16.161 --> 00:07:19.081
Thank you. I have no idea what that means.

00:07:19.164 --> 00:07:21.041
You got a death wish, Professor.

00:07:21.124 --> 00:07:23.418
Something must've happened
in your life that hurt you,

00:07:23.502 --> 00:07:24.503
just like us.

00:07:24.836 --> 00:07:27.839
In my case, it was verbal abuse.

00:07:27.923 --> 00:07:30.050
That's in the rearview mirror, baby.

00:07:30.133 --> 00:07:32.302
It wasn't what he said that hurt,

00:07:32.386 --> 00:07:35.013
it was what was left unsaid.

00:07:35.097 --> 00:07:38.266
Sometimes the best way
to deal with your problems

00:07:38.350 --> 00:07:40.727
is to drive away from them real fast.

00:07:41.144 --> 00:07:43.522
So, yo, you wanna hook up with our crew?

00:07:47.317 --> 00:07:50.320
Again, no idea what that means.

00:07:56.034 --> 00:07:57.619
Good news, everyone!

00:07:57.703 --> 00:08:01.581
Our safe new ship has arrived,
and it's gonna knock your socks on...

00:08:01.665 --> 00:08:02.708
where they belong.

00:08:03.041 --> 00:08:04.042
Ta-da!

00:08:05.836 --> 00:08:08.171
Ooh. Ah.

00:08:08.672 --> 00:08:10.007
Is it inside that box?

00:08:10.090 --> 00:08:11.633
No. That's the ship.

00:08:11.717 --> 00:08:14.511
The boxy shape keeps it
from going too fast.

00:08:14.594 --> 00:08:16.513
And check out the interior.

00:08:18.682 --> 00:08:20.851
Note the rear-facing safety seats.

00:08:20.934 --> 00:08:22.144
Cool!

00:08:23.687 --> 00:08:26.982
Hey, wait. If I'm backwards,
I can't see out the windshield.

00:08:27.065 --> 00:08:28.609
There is no windshield.

00:08:28.692 --> 00:08:30.777
Who needs a big, breakable piece of glass

00:08:30.861 --> 00:08:34.323
when we can just monitor everything
on the padded dashboard display?

00:08:36.283 --> 00:08:38.076
At least there's a cup holder.

00:08:38.160 --> 00:08:39.453
That's an arm holder.

00:08:39.536 --> 00:08:41.705
Hey!

00:08:41.788 --> 00:08:43.582
Well, let's break this ship in.

00:08:43.665 --> 00:08:46.084
This package is going to Glorionimous 3,

00:08:46.168 --> 00:08:49.379
which orbits an incredible
rainbow giant star.

00:08:49.463 --> 00:08:50.756
All right!

00:08:50.839 --> 00:08:51.840
Let's ride!

00:09:09.433 --> 00:09:10.517
Safe and sound.

00:09:10.601 --> 00:09:13.353
Bender is bored, Bender is bored

00:09:13.437 --> 00:09:14.688
Bender, Bender, Bender...

00:09:14.771 --> 00:09:16.940
Leela, Bender's bothering me!

00:09:17.024 --> 00:09:18.859
Driver distraction detected.

00:09:18.942 --> 00:09:20.819
Bender, Bender, Bender

00:09:32.497 --> 00:09:33.749
Amazing!

00:09:33.832 --> 00:09:37.836
You multicultural punks
just race and tinker all day long?

00:09:37.920 --> 00:09:39.504
And we rap about our problems.

00:09:39.588 --> 00:09:41.381
Like my aunt's neighbor is a hoarder.

00:09:41.465 --> 00:09:43.258
Stack of magazines fell on her cat.

00:09:43.592 --> 00:09:45.469
It's hard, you know?

00:09:45.552 --> 00:09:47.429
Yo, you're not alone.

00:09:47.512 --> 00:09:50.307
Hey, Professor,
that dimensional drift was hot!

00:09:50.390 --> 00:09:51.600
How'd you rock that?

00:09:51.683 --> 00:09:53.060
It's simple, Minx.

00:09:53.644 --> 00:09:56.897
All you need is a 4-D intake manifold.

00:10:00.275 --> 00:10:04.363
It sucks in fourth dimension,
creating a friction-less wormhole.

00:10:04.446 --> 00:10:05.864
- Whoa!
- Dig that!

00:10:05.948 --> 00:10:08.951
Ain't no thang but a hyperchicken wing.

00:10:12.496 --> 00:10:13.497
What?

00:10:13.956 --> 00:10:15.666
Huh. I guess we're here.

00:10:15.749 --> 00:10:16.917
Let's make the delivery.

00:10:19.628 --> 00:10:21.588
Delivery auto-completed.

00:10:21.672 --> 00:10:23.924
Welcome home, heroes!

00:10:24.007 --> 00:10:25.384
The ship did everything?

00:10:25.467 --> 00:10:27.636
But we didn't have an adventure.

00:10:27.719 --> 00:10:29.137
This is a delivery company.

00:10:29.221 --> 00:10:31.974
We need less adventures,
not more adventures.

00:10:32.057 --> 00:10:36.061
Now come on, let's go to the ready room
and wait for our next assignment.

00:10:42.901 --> 00:10:44.528
- Leela...
- Ready for action, sir!

00:10:44.611 --> 00:10:45.654
Uh, okay.

00:10:46.071 --> 00:10:48.031
I need you to pick up a few groceries.

00:10:48.115 --> 00:10:51.034
Oh, and on the way,
drop off Fry and Bender at karate class.

00:10:51.118 --> 00:10:52.911
Oh, right, it's Wednesday!

00:10:52.995 --> 00:10:54.871
Today we're gonna learn spinny kicks!

00:10:54.955 --> 00:10:56.415
Yay!

00:11:24.443 --> 00:11:26.570
Stop sign in 75 feet.

00:11:26.653 --> 00:11:29.364
Stop sign in 50 feet.

00:11:29.448 --> 00:11:31.533
I know how to stop at a stop sign!

00:11:36.747 --> 00:11:39.041
Yo, soccer mom, speed it up!

00:11:39.124 --> 00:11:40.667
Move that lunch bucket!

00:11:42.085 --> 00:11:43.211
Oh, Leela!

00:11:43.295 --> 00:11:44.421
Professor?

00:11:44.504 --> 00:11:46.673
What did you do
to the Planet Express ship?

00:11:46.757 --> 00:11:49.426
And why are you wearing
a leather lab coat?

00:11:49.509 --> 00:11:52.054
Because, unlike you, I'm cool.

00:11:52.137 --> 00:11:55.057
I drive fast late at night
when I should be sleeping.

00:11:55.140 --> 00:11:57.559
But you wouldn't understand.

00:11:57.643 --> 00:12:00.812
I understand
I can still outdrive your saggy ass,

00:12:00.896 --> 00:12:02.522
even in this clunker.

00:12:02.606 --> 00:12:04.191
Ooh!

00:12:04.274 --> 00:12:06.568
That one-eyed housewife called you out!

00:12:06.652 --> 00:12:09.029
When and where, PTA?

00:12:13.158 --> 00:12:15.869
What kind of
glorked up drag strip is this?

00:12:15.953 --> 00:12:17.871
Mobius drag strip, man.

00:12:22.668 --> 00:12:26.338
Okay, no cops, no laws, no rules.

00:12:26.421 --> 00:12:27.798
Now here are the rules.

00:12:27.881 --> 00:12:30.592
Once around both same-sides
of the half-twist

00:12:30.676 --> 00:12:32.511
and back to the starting finish line.

00:12:32.594 --> 00:12:33.595
Ready?

00:12:36.223 --> 00:12:38.767
Leela, Professor, don't do this!

00:12:38.850 --> 00:12:40.269
It's too exciting!

00:12:40.352 --> 00:12:42.604
Mark, set...

00:12:43.272 --> 00:12:44.273
go, yo!

00:12:58.579 --> 00:12:59.580
One more lap!

00:12:59.788 --> 00:13:01.290
Nah, half a lap.

00:13:01.373 --> 00:13:04.209
You forgot, on a Mobius strip,
two laps is one lap.

00:13:05.419 --> 00:13:07.588
You kids and your topology.

00:13:14.511 --> 00:13:16.388
The lady from work is winning!

00:13:17.556 --> 00:13:20.684
Looks like you're about to lose
to a minivan.

00:13:20.767 --> 00:13:23.812
Unless you have any surprise moves
you've forgotten about.

00:13:23.896 --> 00:13:26.440
No, no. Wait!

00:13:26.523 --> 00:13:28.025
Dimensional drift!

00:13:43.957 --> 00:13:45.667
Now who's in the lead?

00:13:46.251 --> 00:13:48.587
Seriously, I have no idea.

00:14:02.476 --> 00:14:04.686
Hooray! A tie!

00:14:10.859 --> 00:14:13.362
Do you think they're dead?

00:14:13.445 --> 00:14:17.908
No, no. I choose to believe
they're alive in some other dimension.

00:14:17.991 --> 00:14:19.534
Screaming in agony.

00:14:19.618 --> 00:14:21.954
I hope so.

00:14:30.295 --> 00:14:31.546
What's going on?

00:14:32.005 --> 00:14:34.466
Why do I look like
a stupid cartoon character?

00:14:34.549 --> 00:14:36.301
I feel like I lost weight.

00:14:36.385 --> 00:14:38.095
- All of it.
- Remarkable!

00:14:38.178 --> 00:14:41.056
It seems that colliding
at relativistic speed

00:14:41.139 --> 00:14:44.184
has collapsed us down into two dimensions.

00:14:44.268 --> 00:14:46.103
Oh, no! Like Flatland?

00:14:46.186 --> 00:14:47.521
Call it what you will.

00:14:47.604 --> 00:14:51.191
The point is, the new Shrek movie
won't look nearly as good.

00:14:51.775 --> 00:14:53.902
I was taking a nap in the back seat.

00:14:53.986 --> 00:14:55.320
Anything happen while I was...

00:15:01.493 --> 00:15:03.662
Bloods on the Mobius strip.

00:15:03.745 --> 00:15:05.706
When will these kids learns?

00:15:09.585 --> 00:15:11.920
So now what happens?

00:15:12.004 --> 00:15:15.048
It's the end of Planet Express
and life as we know it.

00:15:15.132 --> 00:15:17.676
We're out of business
unless we find a new crew!

00:15:17.759 --> 00:15:19.803
Yo, dawg, we're a crew.

00:15:19.887 --> 00:15:21.096
Well, that solves that.

00:15:21.638 --> 00:15:25.350
If we're gonna be co-workers,
I got to be straight with you.

00:15:25.434 --> 00:15:31.148
I've been emotionally scarred
by years of unspoken verbal abuse.

00:15:31.773 --> 00:15:32.983
I'm Zoidberg.

00:15:33.066 --> 00:15:35.027
Nice to meet you!

00:15:35.861 --> 00:15:38.906
Hey, Flatso, how do we get out
of this two-bit dimension?

00:15:38.989 --> 00:15:40.866
There's a simple answer for that.

00:15:40.949 --> 00:15:41.992
We can't.

00:15:43.160 --> 00:15:44.536
But on the upside,

00:15:44.620 --> 00:15:49.875
we've got a whole dimension to explore
with entirely different laws of physics.

00:15:49.958 --> 00:15:52.878
Why, watch what happens
when I drop this marble.

00:15:55.881 --> 00:15:59.051
Well, that's the same,
but other things are different.

00:15:59.134 --> 00:16:01.887
Come, look at this
two-dimensional bird's nest.

00:16:01.970 --> 00:16:03.055
Ooh, me first!

00:16:03.138 --> 00:16:04.890
I'll just step past Leela here.

00:16:04.973 --> 00:16:06.266
- Ow!
- Ow!

00:16:06.350 --> 00:16:08.685
You can't step past in this dimension.

00:16:08.769 --> 00:16:10.562
You have to step around.

00:16:14.107 --> 00:16:16.610
Observe this two-dimensional egg.

00:16:16.693 --> 00:16:19.488
If we were in the third dimension,
looking down,

00:16:19.571 --> 00:16:22.157
we'd be able to see
an unhatched chick in it,

00:16:22.241 --> 00:16:24.910
just as a chick inside
a three-dimensional egg

00:16:24.993 --> 00:16:27.788
could be seen by an observer
in the fourth dimension.

00:16:27.871 --> 00:16:29.081
Fourth dimension?

00:16:29.164 --> 00:16:31.124
I can't picture that! You're dumb.

00:16:31.208 --> 00:16:33.126
Halt!

00:16:33.210 --> 00:16:34.211
Who said that?

00:16:34.294 --> 00:16:36.838
All I see are a bunch
of vertical line segments.

00:16:36.922 --> 00:16:38.924
We are the Lords of Flatbush.

00:16:39.007 --> 00:16:41.593
Come. The king has declared a feast
in your honor.

00:16:41.677 --> 00:16:44.179
Wow. How did he even know we're here?

00:16:44.263 --> 00:16:45.889
'Cause I'm him. Let's eat.

00:17:04.866 --> 00:17:06.285
The feast is served!

00:17:06.368 --> 00:17:08.662
Choose whatever two-dimensional foods
you like.

00:17:08.745 --> 00:17:11.373
Crepes, flatbread, McDonald's hamburgers.

00:17:11.456 --> 00:17:12.541
You get the idea.

00:17:12.624 --> 00:17:14.585
Yum! Apples!

00:17:18.505 --> 00:17:20.966
Hey, how come I can't swallow?

00:17:21.049 --> 00:17:22.843
Hmm. I guess it's because

00:17:22.926 --> 00:17:26.597
our two-ended digestive system
can't exist in this dimension.

00:17:26.680 --> 00:17:28.891
I suppose that could be an issue.

00:17:30.893 --> 00:17:33.478
I knew it.
I knew he'd get us killed somehow.

00:17:33.562 --> 00:17:36.106
As you can see, or rather can't see,

00:17:36.189 --> 00:17:37.691
but take my word for it,

00:17:37.774 --> 00:17:42.738
such a digestive system would divide
a 2-D being into separate pieces!

00:17:43.196 --> 00:17:45.324
So how are we supposed to eat and digest?

00:17:50.996 --> 00:17:51.997
Got it.

00:17:52.122 --> 00:17:54.875
Well, since we have
no digestive systems here,

00:17:54.958 --> 00:17:58.545
I guess we'd better get back
to the third dimension after all.

00:17:58.629 --> 00:18:00.756
Third dimension? I can't picture that!

00:18:00.839 --> 00:18:01.840
You're dumb.

00:18:04.635 --> 00:18:06.720
There's nothing funny about science!

00:18:06.803 --> 00:18:09.306
If there can be an X-axis and a Y-axis,

00:18:09.389 --> 00:18:10.891
why not a Z-axis?

00:18:10.974 --> 00:18:13.727
He's opening our minds to new ideas!

00:18:13.810 --> 00:18:14.811
Kill him!

00:18:24.571 --> 00:18:26.198
- To the ship!
- Which ship?

00:18:26.281 --> 00:18:28.033
Leela's! It's safer.

00:18:28.116 --> 00:18:30.077
Safety kills. We got to move!

00:18:37.125 --> 00:18:38.961
Let's go! Let's go! Let's go!

00:18:39.711 --> 00:18:42.047
Oh, what's the point of fleeing?

00:18:42.130 --> 00:18:44.132
Even if we escape from those creatures,

00:18:44.216 --> 00:18:47.219
we'll still be stuck in this dimension
till we starve.

00:18:47.302 --> 00:18:49.555
Wait. What about a dimensional drift?

00:18:49.638 --> 00:18:51.932
If it went through
the fourth dimension before,

00:18:52.015 --> 00:18:54.351
maybe here,
it'll go through the third dimension!

00:18:54.434 --> 00:18:56.144
By God, you're right!

00:18:56.228 --> 00:18:58.564
But to keep us there,
I'd need to accelerate

00:18:58.647 --> 00:19:02.025
to dimensional escape velocity
during the drift.

00:19:02.109 --> 00:19:04.528
Oh, if only Minx could see that.

00:19:04.611 --> 00:19:08.115
Then she'd see me
as more than just a father figure.

00:19:18.875 --> 00:19:19.876
Now's good.

00:19:30.637 --> 00:19:32.264
Two point one dimensions!

00:19:32.347 --> 00:19:33.473
Two point two!

00:19:33.557 --> 00:19:35.392
Two point pi!

00:19:35.475 --> 00:19:37.686
Look, up there! There's some up!

00:19:37.769 --> 00:19:39.062
The third dimension!

00:19:39.146 --> 00:19:43.317
Indeed, but we're about to crash
into some sort of huge disk!

00:19:45.694 --> 00:19:48.113
My bowels returned at a bad time!

00:19:51.366 --> 00:19:53.744
I'd likes to say a few words.

00:19:55.704 --> 00:19:57.122
I'm gonna burns them ups.

00:20:28.153 --> 00:20:29.196
We're back, baby!

00:20:31.740 --> 00:20:34.576
It's been an emotional five minutes,

00:20:34.660 --> 00:20:36.995
but I guess everything worked out
in the end.

00:20:37.079 --> 00:20:39.414
Yo, boss, not everything.

00:20:47.589 --> 00:20:48.590
Hello?

00:20:49.508 --> 00:20:50.509
Dad?